[size=5][b]psi_autocast: one-key psi casting[/b][/size]

Press one key: your character draws the psi amp, selects the discipline and casts it. No F-key cycling, no clicking, no overload-bar timing.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Works from any weapon.[/b] The key draws the amp, waits for it to come up, then casts. With the amp already out, it casts immediately.
[*][b]Scripts for all 35 disciplines[/b], two per discipline:
[list]
[*][b]Quickfire[/b] ([i]T1_Projected_Cryokinesis_Quickfire[/i]): casts immediately.
[*][b]Conditional overload[/b] ([i]T1_Projected_Cryokinesis[/i]): overloads when the discipline benefits from it, otherwise casts immediately and says why.
[/list]
[*][b]Overload timing from the game's own data.[/b] The release time is worked out on every cast from the discipline's tier and your current PSI, using the game's Overload Params table. It adapts as your PSI rises.
[*][b]Chains:[/b] one key can cast several disciplines in a row, each following its own quickfire or overload rule.
[*][b]Console feedback:[/b] every cast reports its tier, your pre-overload PSI, the overload zone and its decision.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Macro Builder[/b][/size]
The easiest way to make your own macros: open [b]psi\Macro_Builder.html[/b] from the download in your browser (it works offline), or use the online copy at [url=https://feygon.github.io/SS2PsiAutocast/Macro_Builder.html]feygon.github.io/SS2PsiAutocast[/url].
[list]
[*]Pick a discipline and choose [b]conditional overload[/b] or [b]quickfire[/b], then add as many casts as you like, in order.
[*]It starts with an [b]Arm psi amp[/b] step, which you can remove, and puts a 500 ms wait between steps. That's the psi amp's refire limit, and it won't let two casts go closer together than that.
[*]Round off a macro with a [b]psi hypo[/b] anywhere in it, and finish with a [b]weapon switch[/b]: back to your previous weapon, or to any weapon by name.
[*][b]Auto psi hypo:[/b] tick one box, and before each cast the macro uses a psi hypo if your psi points are at or below your maximum minus what a hypo restores, so a hypo is never wasted. It reads your difficulty (30 on Easy, 20 otherwise) and the Pharmo-Friendly upgrade (+20%) itself.
[*]It gives you the finished macro file (download or copy) and the exact key binding line for user.bnd, with install steps.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Write your own macros[/b][/size]
Every script is a small text file built from shared parts, so you can make your own in Notepad, with no modding tools. A macro is a few [i]set[/i] lines plus calls to the parts in [i]psi\lib[/i]:
[code]set psi_name T1_Projected_Cryokinesis
set psi_power 6
set psi_slot 0
set psi_benefits 1
run psi\lib\T1.cmd
run psi\lib\overload.cmd
run psi\lib\draw_cast.cmd[/code]
[list]
[*][b]T1.cmd to T5.cmd[/b] set the discipline's tier.
[*][b]quickfire.cmd[/b] or [b]overload.cmd[/b] chooses how it casts.
[*][b]draw_cast.cmd[/b] draws the amp if needed, then casts.
[/list]
Chain macros cast several disciplines from one key. This is the format the Macro Builder writes: [i]arm[/i] draws the amp, [i]6o[/i] is discipline 6 with conditional overload, [i]15q[/i] is discipline 15 quickfired, and [i]w500[/i] waits 500 ms:
[code]set psi_chain arm,6o,w500,15q
set psi_draw_ms 800
set psi_chain_gap_ms 500
summon_obj PsiChain[/code]
Macros are read fresh on every keypress, so you can edit them while the game is running. The readme lists every setting and every discipline number.

[b]You can also have Claude write macros for you.[/b] The download includes [i]psi\psi_autocast_MACROS_FOR_CLAUDE.md[/i], a guide to the inner workings written for Claude: the macro format, every setting, the overload math, the discipline numbers and the rules a macro must follow. Give Claude that file, describe the macro you want, and it can write the file and tell you how to bind it to a key.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]System Shock 2: 25th Anniversary Remaster on PC. Tested on the Epic version, game version 1.3.4984.
[*]Won't work on the classic 1999 version.
[*]Tested alongside the remaster's bundled mods (SCP beta 6, SHTUP, Four Hundred, patch_ext). Multiplayer is untested.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into the game's install folder (the one containing SystemShock2Remastered.exe). This creates [i]mods\psi_autocast.kpf[/i] and a [i]psi[/i] folder of scripts.
[*]New Game → Mods → add [b]psi_autocast[/b] → Apply → start. Once the first level loads, load your own save, then make a regular save. [b]Don't use mod_apply mid-game[/b]: it can unload the level.
[*]Close the game, open [i]%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\Nightdive Studios\System Shock 2 Remastered\user.bnd[/i] in Notepad, and add one line per key, for example:
[code]bind g "run psi\T1_Projected_Cryokinesis_Quickfire.cmd"
bind j "run psi\T1_Projected_Cryokinesis.cmd"[/code]
[/list]

The included readme lists every script, how the overload timing is calculated, how to build your own scripts and chains, and a troubleshooting table.

